t false, isfirstOptionDefault true, isQueryParam false? Usually filters should be query params? The base template has isQueryParam false. But maybe we want them to be query params? The user didn't specify. We'll keep default.\n\nWe need an apiUrl for filters. The template says filters.apiUrl: endpoint used to fetch dropdown filter options. We need to set a placeholder. We can use \"http://localhost:8085/api/v1/highway/filters\" or similar. Since not specified, we can use a generic placeholder: \"http://localhost:8085/api/v1/highway/filters\". We'll set that.\n\nWidgets:\n\nNumber-stat KPIs: 3 widgets: Sales($), Opportunity ($), Opportunity (%). All formatted with currency prefix ($). But Opportunity (%) is a percentage, not currency. But user says formatted with currency prefix ($). Maybe they want all with $ prefix. We'll follow instruction: all KPIs must be formatted with a currency prefix ($). So even Opportunity (%) will have $ prefix? That seems odd but we follow.\n\nWe need to create 3 number-stats widgets. Use base config for number_stats. We'll modify title, key, value, prefix, useFormatStat true, useQueryParams true. For each widget, we need unique widgetId: widget1, widget2, widget3.\n\nWe need to set class for each widget. They are number-stats. Row1 will contain 3 widgets. According to rules: 3 widgets in row =\u003e class = \"col-12 col-sm-6 col-md-4 col-lg-4\" for each. So each widget's class should be that.\n\nWe need to set apiUrl for each widget. Base config uses \"http://localhost:8085/api/v1/highway/financial-summary\". We can keep same for all? But maybe each KPI uses same endpoint. We'll keep same.\n\nWe need to set key and value. Base config has key \"opportunity\", value \"data\". For Sales($) we might use key \"sales\" and value \"data\". For Opportunity ($) key \"opportunity\" value \"data\". For Opportunity (%) key \"opportunity_percent\" value \"data\". But we need to ensure data binding. We'll set key accordingly.\n\nWe need to set prefix