a.category\",\n          \"series\": \"data.value\",\n          \"orientation\": \"right\",\n          \"barColor\": \"#D3D3D3\",\n          \"useQueryParams\": true,\n          \"useFormatStat\": true,\n          \"useCommaStat\": true,\n          \"filterKey\": \"application_id\",\n          \"filterListner\": [\n            \"auto\"\n          ],\n          \"triggerFilterEvent\": true,\n          \"tooltipLabels\": {\n            \"category\": \"Segment\",\n            \"value\": \"Opportunity $\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"widgetId\": \"widget6\",\n          \"type\": \"horizontal-bar-chart\",\n          \"title\": \"Sales by Segment\",\n          \"class\": \"col-12 col-sm-12 col-md-6 col-lg-6\",\n          \"apiUrl\": \"http://localhost:8085/api/v1/highway/sales-summary\",\n          \"xAxis\": \"data.value\",\n          \"yAxis\": \"data.category\",\n          \"series\": \"data.value\",\n          \"orientation\": \"right\",\n          \"barColor\": \"#D3D3D3\",\n          \"useQueryParams\": true,\n          \"useFormatStat\": true,\n          \"useCommaStat\": true,\n          \"filterKey\": \"application_id\",\n          \"filterListner\": [\n            \"auto\"\n          ],\n          \"triggerFilterEvent\": true,\n          \"tooltipLabels\": {\n            \"category\": \"Segment\",\n            \"value\": \"Sales $\"\n          }\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","thinking":"The user wants full JSON. That triggers FINALIZATION MODE. We must output the full DVM JSON. We need to create filters for each dropdown. Use base filter template. For each filter: name, key, options, type dropdown, isMultiSelect? Not specified; default false? Probably single select. isfirstOptionDefault true. isQueryParam false? Might be true? Not specified. We'll keep defaults.\n\nWe need API URL for filters: unspecified. We can set a placeholder like \"http://localhost:8085/api/v1/filters\". But we need consistent with widgets. The widgets use http://localhost:8085/api/v1/highway/... We'll set filters.apiUrl to \"http://localhost:8085/api/v1/highway/filters\" maybe. But not specified. We'll use \"http://localhost:8085/api/v1/highway/filters\".\n\nNumber-stat widgets: three. Use base number_stats template. Need to modify title, key, value? The base uses key \"opportunity\". For Sales($) and Opportunity($) and Opportunity(%). We need separate keys. For Sales($) maybe key \"sales\". For Opportunity($) key \"opportunity\". For Opportunity(%) key \"opportunity_percent\". Use same apiUrl? The base uses financial-summary. We'll keep same apiUrl for all three. Use prefix \"$\" for all. For Opportunity(%) maybe no prefix? But requirement says all KPIs formatted with currency prefix ($). So even percent? Might be weird but follow. Use prefix \"$\". Use useFormatStat true. useQueryParams true.\n\nWe need unique widgetIds: widget1, widget2, widget3 for KPIs.\n\nClass: number-stats row has 3 widgets. According to rules: 3 widgets =\u003e class \"col-12 col-sm-6 col-md-4 col-lg-4\" for each. So set class accordingly.\n\nChart components: Treemap Chart: use base treemap_chart. Title \"Opportunity by Segment and Customer\". Use same apiUrl as base. Need to set filterKey? Base has filterKey [\"application_id\"]. We might not need. We'll keep as is. Use widgetId widget4. Class: base has \"col-12 col-md-6 col-sm-12 col-lg-6\". But we need to adjust class based on row layout. We will put treemap in its own row? We can put treemap and horizontal bar charts in same row? The requirement: \"Treemap Chart: Opportunity by Segment and Customer\" and two horizontal bar charts. We can put treemap in row2, and horizontal bars in row3. Or combine treemap and one bar in same row? Simpler: row2: treemap. row3: two horizontal bars. For horizontal bar charts: base horizontal-bar-chart. We need two instances: one for Opportunity($) by Segment, one for Sales by Segment. Titles accordingly. Use same apiUrl? Base uses sales-summary. For Opportun