Region, DBU/EBU Direct, Engine Model, Certification, Segment, Sub-Segment, Customer Type, Customer Name, AEX, and Customer Spec.\n\nNumber-Stat KPIs:\nAdd three number-stat widgets —\nSales($), Opportunity ($), and Opportunity (%).\nAll KPIs must be formatted with a currency prefix ($) and support query parameters for dynamic updates.\n\nChart Components:\nInclude the following visualization charts —\n\nTreemap Chart: Opportunity by Segment and Customer (showing data hierarchy between Segment and Customer).\n\nHorizontal Bar Chart: Opportunity($) by Segment.\n\nHorizontal Bar Chart: Sales by Segment.', 'images': []}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I will ask clarifying questions about API URLs, data keys, filter options, multi-select, query param, filter listeners, and layout.Great! Let’s fine‑tune the details so the dashboard works exactly as you want.\n\n**1. API Endpoints & Data Keys**\n\n| Widget / Filter | Suggested API URL (current default) | Data key(s) you’d like to use |\n|-----------------|-------------------------------------|------------------------------|\n| **Filters** | `http://localhost:8085/api/v1/highway/filter-options` | e.g., `region`, `dbu_ebu_direct`, `engine_model`, … |\n| **Number‑Stats** | `http://localhost:8085/api/v1/highway/financial-summary` | `sales`, `opportunity`, `opportunity_percent` |\n| **Treemap Chart** | `http://localhost:8085/api/v1/highway/grouped-dropdown` | `segment`, `customer_name`, `opportunity` |\n| **Horizontal Bar – Opportunity** | `http://localhost:8085/api/v1/highway/opportunity-summary` | `segment`, `opportunity` |\n| **Horizontal Bar – Sales** | `http://localhost:8085/api/v1/highway/sales-summary` | `segment`, `sales` |\n\n> **Questions**  \n> • Do you want to keep these URLs or provide custom ones?  \n> • Are the data keys above correct, or should they be changed?  \n\n**2. Filter Settings**\n\n| Filter | Key (snake_case) | Options key | Multi‑select? | Default first option? | Query param? |\n|--------|------------------|-------------|---------------|-----------------------|--------------|\n| Region | `region` | `region` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |\n| DBU/EBU Direct | `dbu_ebu_direct` | `dbu_ebu_direct` | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |\n| Engine Model | `engine_model` | `engine_model` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |\n| Certification | `certification` | `certification` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |\n| Segment | `segment` | `segment` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |\n| Sub‑Segment | `sub_segment` | `sub_segment` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |\n| Customer Type | `customer_type` | `customer_type` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |\n| Customer Name | `customer_name` | `customer_name` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |\n| AEX | `aex` | `aex` | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |\n| Customer Spec | `customer_spec` | `customer_spec` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |\n\n> **Questions**  \n> • Are these multi‑select settings correct?  \n> • Do you want any filter to be *not* a query param?  \n\n**3. Widget‑Filter Relationships**\n\n- All widgets should listen to **all** filters (so they update when any filter changes).  \n- For the treemap chart, you might want to filter by `segment` and `customer_name`.  \n- For the horizontal bar charts, filter by `segment` (and optionally `region`).\n\n> **Questions**  \n> • Should any widget ignore certain filters?  \n> • Do you want the treemap to trigger filter events for the bar charts?  \n\n**4. Layout**\n\n- **Row 1**: 3 number‑stat widgets (Sales, Opportunity, Opportunity\u202f%) – each gets `col-12 col-sm-6 col-md-4 col-lg-4`.  \n- **Row 2**: Treemap chart – full width (`col-12`).  \n- **Row 3**: Two horizontal bar charts side by side – each `col-12 col-sm-12 col-md-6 col-lg-6`.\n\n> **Questions**  \n> • Does this layout look good to you, or would you prefer a different arrangement?  \n\nLet me know your preferences or any corrections, and we’ll lock in the design!', 'images': []}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'No generate final \njson', 'images': []}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Got it—no final JSON yet.  \nLet me know if you’d like to tweak any of the details (API URLs, data keys, filter settings, layout, etc.) or i