ats, so default rule: 1 widget =\u003e class \"col-12 col-sm-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12\". But base config has class \"col-12 col-md-6 col-sm-12 col-lg-6\". We override to new class. Also need apiUrl: base is \"/api/v1/highway/grouped-dropdown\". Use that. filterKey: [\"application_id\"]? But we have filters. We might need to set filterKey to list of filter keys? The base has filterKey [\"application_id\"]. But we might want to trigger filter events. We'll keep as base. filterListner: [\"auto\"]. triggerFilterEvent true. tooltipLabels as base.\n\nRow2: Widgets 2-4: Three number-stats KPIs: Sales Opportunity ($), Opportunity ($), Opportunity (%). We need three widgets. Each is number-stats type. For number-stats, class depends on number of widgets in row: 3 widgets =\u003e class \"col-12 col-sm-6 col-md-4 col-lg-4\". So each widget gets that class. Need unique widgetIds widget2, widget3, widget4. Titles: \"Sales Opportunity ($)\", \"Opportunity ($)\", \"Opportunity (%)\". Need to set key, value, etc. Base config has key \"opportunity\", value \"data\", title \"Opportunity ($)\". We need to adjust. For Sales Opportunity ($), maybe key \"sales_opportunity\"? value \"data\"? Might need to set prefix \"$\". For Opportunity (%), maybe key \"opportunity_percent\", value \"data\", prefix \"\"? Use useFormatStat true. UseQueryParams true. Use same apiUrl? Base uses \"/api/v1/highway/financial-summary\". We'll keep that. For each, we might need to set filterKey? Not specified. We'll keep base.\n\nRow3: Widgets 6-7: Two horizontal bar charts: Opportunity ($) by Segment and Sales by Segment. Base horizontal-bar-chart has title \"Sales by Segment\". We'll create two widgets: widget5? Wait numbering: we used widget2-4 for row2. Next widget id widget5 for first horizontal bar chart, widget6 for second. Titles: \"Opportunity ($) by Segment\" and \"Sales by Segment\". Need to adjust xAxis, yAxis, series? Base uses xAxis \"data.value\", yAxis \"data.category\", series \"data.value\". For