ches this type and purpose, you should start from this base config, modify fields (such as title, apiUrl, data bindings, filter listeners, etc.) to match the user\'s description, and ensure `widgetId` is set to a unique value.\n\n\nWidget key: line_chart\n\nWidget type (from config.type): line-chart\n\nBase config JSON:\n\n{\n  "widgetId": "widget5",\n  "type": "line-chart",\n  "title": "Revenue Growth",\n  "class": "col-12 col-md-6 col-sm-12 col-lg-4",\n  "apiUrl": "assets/charts-config/line-chart-config.json",\n  "xAxis": "data.category",\n  "yAxis": "value",\n  "series": "data.value",\n  "useQueryParams": false\n}\n\n\nUsage notes: This widget is defined in widgets.json and has the type shown above. Whenever the user requests this widget key explicitly, or describes a component that matches this type and purpose, you should start from this base config, modify fields (such as title, apiUrl, data bindings, filter listeners, etc.) to match the user\'s description, and ensure `widgetId` is set to a unique value.\n\n\nWidget key: bar_chart\n\nWidget type (from config.type): bar-chart\n\nBase config JSON:\n\n{\n  "widgetId": "widget6",\n  "type": "bar-chart",\n  "title": "Sales Overview",\n  "class": "col-12 col-md-6 col-sm-12 col-lg-4",\n  "apiUrl": "assets/charts-config/bar-chart-config.json",\n  "xAxis": "data.category",\n  "yAxis": "value",\n  "series": "data.value",\n  "useQueryParams": false\n}\n\n\nUsage notes: This widget is defined in widgets.json and has the type shown above. Whenever the user requests this widget key explicitly, or describes a component that matches this type and purpose, you should start from this base config, modify fields (such as title, apiUrl, data bindings, filter listeners, etc.) to match the user\'s description, and ensure `widgetId` is set to a unique value.\n\n\nWidget key: bubble_chart\n\nWidget type (from config.type): bubble-chart\n\nBase config JSON:\n\n{\n  "widgetId": "widget7",\n  "type": "bubble-chart",\n  "title": "GDP Gro