ion, segment, sub_segment, customer_type, customer_name, aex, customer_spec.\n\nNow widgets.\n\nRow 1: Widget 1: Treemap Chart — Opportunity by Segment and Customer. Use treemap_chart template. Title: \"Opportunity by Segment and Customer\". API URL: from template: \"/api/v1/highway/grouped-dropdown\". We might keep same. filterKey: [\"application_id\"]? But we might need to adapt? The user didn't specify filters. We can keep default. But we need to set widgetId unique: widget1. class: need to compute based on row count. Row 1 has 1 widget. For number-stats rule? But this is treemap-chart, not number-stats. For non-number-stats, if 1 widget: class = \"col-12 col-sm-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12\". So set class accordingly.\n\nRow 2: Widgets 2-5: Three Number-Stat KPIs — Sales Opportunity ($), Opportunity ($), Opportunity (%). So we need three number-stats widgets. Use number_stats template. We need to modify title and maybe apiUrl? The base uses \"/api/v1/highway/financial-summary\". We can keep same. But we might need to differentiate data binding? The base has key \"opportunity\", value \"data\". For each KPI, we might need to set key differently? But we can keep same key? But we need unique widgetId. For each widget, we need to set class based on row count. Row 2 has 3 widgets. For number-stats, rule: 3 widgets =\u003e class = \"col-12 col-sm-6 col-md-4 col-lg-4\". So each widget gets that class.\n\nWe need to set titles: \"Sales Opportunity ($)\", \"Opportunity ($)\", \"Opportunity (%)\". For the last one, maybe prefix? The base has prefix \"$\". For percentage, maybe no prefix. We can set prefix \"\" or maybe \"%\" but not needed. We can keep prefix \"$\" for first two, and for third maybe prefix \"\" and use useFormatStat? The base has useFormatStat true. For percentage, maybe useFormatStat true but we might want to set useFormatStat true and maybe useCommaStat? Not necessary. We'll keep base.\n\nWe need to set widgetId: widget2, widget3, widget4.\n\nRow 3: Widgets 6-7: Two Horizontal Bar Charts — Opportunity ($) by Segment and Sales by Segment. Use horizontal-bar-chart template. Titles: \"Opportunity ($) by Segment\" and \"Sales by Segment\". API URL: base uses \"/api/v1/highway/sales-summary\". For Opportunity ($) by Segment, maybe same API? Might need different endpoint. But we can keep same. For Sales by Segment, same. We can keep same. For each widget, set widgetId: widget5, widget6. Row 3 has 2 widgets. For non-number-stats, 2 widgets =\u003e class = \"col-12 col-sm-12 col-md-6 col-lg-6\". So each gets that.\n\nWe need to ensure unique widgetIds across all widgets: widget1, widget2, widget3, widget4, widget5, widget6.\n\nNow filters.apiUrl: we need to set an endpoint for fetching dropdown options. The template says \"apiUrl\": \"\u003cstring\u003e\" but not specified. We can set a placeholder like \"/api/v1/filters\". But maybe we need to use a generic endpoint. Since not specified, we can set \"/api/v1/filters\". Or maybe \"/api/v1/filter-options\". We'll choose \"/api/v1/filters\".\n\nNow build final JSON.\n\nLet's construct.\n\n{\n  \"dashboard-name\": \"Demo Version\",\n  \"filters\": {\n    \"apiUrl\": \"/api/v1/filters\",\n    \"content\": [\n      { \"name\": \"Region\", \"key\": \"region\", \"options\": \"region\", \"type\": \"dropdown\", \"isMultiSelect\": true, \"isfirstOptionDefault\": true, \"isQueryParam\": false },\n      { \"name\": \"DBU/EBU Direct\", \"key\": \"dbu_ebu_direct\", \"options\": \"dbu_ebu_direct\", \"type\": \"dropdown\", \"isMultiSelect\": true, \"isfirstOptionDefault\": true, \"isQueryParam\": false },\n      { \"name\": \"Engine Model\", \"key\": \"engine_model\", \"options\": \"engine_model\", \"type\": \"dropdown\", \"isMultiSelect\": true, \"isfirstOptionDefault\": true, \"isQueryParam\": false },\n      { \"name\": \"Certification\", \"key\": \"certification\", \"options\": \"certification\", \"type\": \"dropdown\", \"isMultiSelect\": true, \"isfirstOptionDefault\": true, \"isQueryParam\": false },\n      { \"name\": \"Segment\", \"key\": \"segment\", \"options\": \"segment\", \"type\": \"dropdown\", \"isMultiSelect\": true, \"isfirstOptionDefault\": true, \"isQueryParam\": false },\n      { \"name\": \"Sub-Segment\", \"key\": \"sub_segment\", \"options\": \"sub_segment\", \"type\": \"dropdown\", \"isMultiSelect\": true, \"isfirstOptionDefault\": true, \"isQueryParam\": false },\n      { \"name\": \"Customer Type\", \"key\": \"customer_type\", \"options\": \"customer_type\", \"type\": \"dropdown\", \"isMultiSelect\": true, \"isfirstOptionDefault\": true, \"isQueryParam\": false },\n      { \"name\": \"Customer Name\", \"key\": \"customer_name\", \"options\": \"customer_name\", \"type\": \"dropdown\", \"isMultiSelect\": true, \"isfirstOptionDefault\": true, \"isQueryParam\": false },\n      { \"name\": \"AEX\", \"key\": \"aex\", \"options\": \"aex\", \"type\": \"dropdown\", \"isMultiSelect\": true, \"isfirstOptionDefault\": true, \"isQueryParam\": false },\n      { \"name\": \"Customer Spec\", \"key\": \"customer_spec\", \"options\": \"customer_spec\", \"type\": \"dropdown\", \"isMultiSelect\": true, \"isfirstOptionDefault\": true, \"isQueryParam\": false }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"pageContent\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"row1\",\n      \"columns\": [\n        {\n          \"widgetId\": \"widget1\",\n          \"type\": \"treemap-chart\",\n          \"title\": \"Opportunity by Segment and Customer\",\n          \"class\": \"col-12 col-sm-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12\",\n          \"apiUrl\": \"/api/v1/highway/grouped-dropdown\",\n          \"series\": \"data\",\n          \"useQueryParams\": true,\n          \"useCommaStat\": true,\n          \"triggerFilterEvent\": true,\n          \"filterKey\": [\"application_id\"],\n          \"filterListner\": [\"auto\"],\n          \"tooltipLabels\": {\n            \"parent\": \"Segment\",\n            \"child\": \"Customer Name\",\n            \"value\": \"Opportunity $\",\n            \"sales\": \"Current Sales $\"\n  