tch the user\'s description, and ensure `widgetId` is set to a unique value.\n\n\nWidget key: stack_bar_chart\n\nWidget type (from config.type): stack-bar-chart\n\nBase config JSON:\n\n{\n  "widgetId": "widget12",\n  "type": "stack-bar-chart",\n  "title": "Product Sales by Category",\n  "class": "col-12 col-md-6 col-sm-12 col-lg-4",\n  "apiUrl": "assets/charts-config/stack-bar-config.json",\n  "xAxis": "data.category",\n  "yAxis": "value",\n  "series": "data.series"\n}\n\n\nUsage notes: This widget is defined in widgets.json and has the type shown above. Whenever the user requests this widget key explicitly, or describes a component that matches this type and purpose, you should start from this base config, modify fields (such as title, apiUrl, data bindings, filter listeners, etc.) to match the user\'s description, and ensure `widgetId` is set to a unique value.\n\n\nWidget key: table_widget\n\nWidget type (from config.type): table\n\nBase config JSON:\n\n{\n  "widgetId": "widgetTable",\n  "type": "table",\n  "title": "cspec-table",\n  "class": "col-12 col-md-5 col-sm-12 col-lg-6",\n  "apiUrl": "/off_highway/dashboard/customerSpec",\n  "headerColumns": [\n    {\n      "key": "option_name",\n      "label": "Option Name"\n    },\n    {\n      "key": "current_option_price",\n      "label": "Current Price($)"\n    },\n    {\n      "key": "proposed_option_price",\n      "label": "Proposed Price($)"\n    },\n    {\n      "key": "difference",\n      "label": "Difference ($)"\n    },\n    {\n      "key": "current_markup",\n      "label": "Current Markup"\n    },\n    {\n      "key": "proposed_markup",\n      "label": "Proposed Markup"\n    }\n  ],\n  "isPagination": true\n}\n\n\nUsage notes: This widget is defined in widgets.json and has the type shown above. Whenever the user requests this widget key explicitly, or describes a component that matches this type and purpose, you should start from this base config, modify fields (such as title, apiUrl, data bindings, filter listeners, etc.) to match the user\'s description, and ensure `widgetId` is set to a unique value.\n\n\nWidget key: drill_through_table\n\nWidget type (from config.type): drill-down\n\nBase config JSON:\n\n{\n  "widgetId": "widget1-2",\n  "type": "drill-down",\n  "title": "Opprtunity by Segment and Customer",\n  "class": "col-12 col-md-10 col-sm-12 col-lg-6",\n  "apiUrl": "/dashboard/impactCustomer",\n  "headers": [\n    {\n      "name": "Customer Name",\n      "expandabile": true,\n      "showTotal": false,\n      "prop": "name",\n      "width": 220\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Engine Model",\n      "expandabile": true,\n      "showTotal": true,\n      "prop": "name",\n      "width": 85\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n\nUsage notes: This widget is defined in widgets.json and has the type shown above. Whenever the user requests this widget key explicitly, or describes a component that matches this type and purpose, you should start from this base config, modify fields (such as title, apiUrl, data bindings, filter listeners, etc.) to match the user\'s description, and ensure `widgetId` is set to a unique value.\n\n\nWidget key: line_column_chart\n\nWidget type (from config.type): line-column-chart\n\nBase config JSON:\n\n{\n  "widgetId": "widget5",\n  "type": "line-column-chart",\n  "title": "Total opportunity Yearly Sales and Percentage change",\n  "class": "col-12 col-md-8 col-lg-8",\n  "apiUrl": "/dashboard/totalOpportunity/cagr",\n  "dataKey": "totalOpportunity",\n  "xAxis": "years",\n  "barSeries": "priceList",\n  "lineSeries": "percentage",\n  "editableLineValues": true,\n  "seriesNames": [\n    "Projected Engine System Sales $",\n    "Opportunity %"\n  ],\n  "yAxisNames": [\n    "Yearly Sales ($)",\n    "Yearly Price Change Percent"\n  ],\n  "useQueryParams": true,\n  "triggerFilterEvent": true\n}\n\n\nUsage notes: This widget is defined in widgets.json and has the type shown above. Whenever the user requests this widget key explicitly, or describes a component that matches this type and purpose, you should start from this base config, modify fields (such as title, apiUrl, data bindings, filter listeners, etc.) to match the user\'s description, and ensure `widgetId` is set to a unique value.\n\n\nWidget key: waterfall_stack_chart\n\nWidget type (from config.type): waterfall-stack\n\nBase config JSON:\n\n{\n  "widgetId": "widget2-1",\n  "type": "waterfall-stack",\n  "title": "Proposed ESP",\n  "class": "col-12 col-md-10 col-sm-12 col-lg-12",\n  "apiUrl": "/dashboard/totalBreakdown",\n  "categories": [\n    "PID",\n    "ACO",\n    "EBU Disc",\n    "CES DN",\n    "CES Disc",\n    "EBU + CES Imp",\n    "DBU Cost",\n    "DBU Mar",\n    "DBU Imp",\n    "Final Prices"\n  ]\n}\n\n\nUsage notes: This widget is defined in widgets.json and has the type shown above. Whenever the user requests this widget key explicitly, or describes a component that matches this type and purpose, you should start from this base config, modify fields (such as title, apiUrl, data bindings, filter listeners, etc.) to match the user\'s description, and ensure `widgetId` is set to a unique value.\n\n\nWidget key: combined_chart\n\nWidget type (from config.type): combined-chart\n\nBase config JSON:\n\n{\n  "widgetId": "widget1-1",\n  "type": "combined-chart",\n  "title": "Opprtunity by Segment and Customer",\n  "class": "col-12 col-md-10 col-sm-12 col-lg-6",\n  "apiUrl": "/price-performance/data",\n  "xAxisLabel": "HP",\n  "yAxisLabel": "ESP(in Ks)",\n  "chartConfig": [\n    {\n      "type": "line",\n      "linecolor": "#424242",\n      "bgcolor": "rgba(66, 66, 66, 0.1)",\n      "name": "NA Proposed Baseline Curve"\n    },\n    {\n      "type": "line",\n      "linecolor": "#00578A",\n      "bgcolor": "rgba(0, 87, 138, 0.1)",\n      "name": "NA DN Baseline"\n    },\n    {\n      "type": "line",\n      "linecolor": "#DA281C",\n      "bgcolor": "rgba(218, 40, 28, 0.1)",\n      "name": "Special Baseline"\n    },\n    {\n      "type": "line",\n      "linecolor": "#738B1F",\n      "bgcolor": "rgba(115, 139, 31, 0.1)",\n      "name": "Strategic Baseline"\n    },\n    {\n      "type": "scatter",\n      "tooltip": "custom",\n      "bubbleColor": "dropdown_customer_category_filter",\n      "name": "Customer Type",\n      "colors": {\n        "Default": "#424242",\n        "Special": "#00578A",\n        "Large": "#DA281C",\n        "EBU Direct": "#738B1F"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  "useQueryParams": true,\n  "filterKey": [\n    "id",\n    "uid_seg_data_link"\n  ],\n  "filterListner": [\n    "widget1-2"\n  ]\n}\n\n\nUsage notes: This widget is defined in widgets.json and has the type shown above. Whenever the user requests this widget key explicitly, or describes a component that matches this type and purpose, you should start from this base config, modify fields (such as title, apiUrl, data bindings, filter listeners, etc.) to match the user\'s description, and ensure `widgetId` is set to a unique value.\n\n\nWidget key: upload_files\n\nWidget type (from config.type): upload-file\n\nBase config JSON:\n\n{\n  "widgetId": "widgetUploadFiles",\n  "type": "upload-file",\n  "class": "col-12 col-md-6 col-lg-12",\n  "title": "Upload Files",\n  "multiple": true,\n  "accept": ".pdf,.docx,.xlsx,.png,.jpg",\n  "renderCondition": {\n    "filter": "action_type",\n    "is": "Upload File"\n  },\n  "dependsOnFilters": [\n    "action_type",\n    "workflowName"\n  ],\n  "actions": [\n    {\n      "label": "Cancel",\n      "apiUrl": "/api/v1/svm/cancel",\n      "showOn": {\n        "filter": "action_type",\n        "is": "Upload File"\n      },\n      "confirmation": {\n        "title": "Confirm Cancellation",\n        "message": "Are you sure you want to cancel? All unsaved changes will be lost."\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      "label": "Upload",\n      "apiUrl": "/api/v1/svm/upload",\n      "showOn": {\n        "filter": "action_type",\n        "is": "Upload File"\n      },\n      "confirmation": {\n        "title": "Confirm Upload",\n        "message": "Are 